Kind: ablation
Issue: #764
Over: 764-widen-console-gap.patch
Takes out: what #764 changed in hello_server -- setvbuf(stdout, NULL, _IONBF, 0) at the top of main() again, so stdout is unbuffered and musl's vfprintf() formats into 80 bytes of its own.  The line arm's 101-byte literal does not fit in the 42 bytes left of them, so musl sends what it holds with the literal, a console write that leaves the line open, before "this one (#764)" is formatted; the widen's line lands in the gap, and scripts/suite-i386.sh never finds the arm's line whole.  __uros_writev() gathering the pieces does not help here: the line is not finished when the first write goes.
Run: i386 -- UROS_BUILD_DIR=<worktree>/uros/build scripts/suite-i386.sh -r bundle-kvm-4, from a worktree with 764-widen-console-gap.patch and this one, and a build of its own; scripts/ablate.sh cannot judge it
Expect: never said: \(hello_server\): console: a line of \[0-9\]\* characters

